# Config file folding

This file anchors VS Code's file-nesting rules: the config files beside it nest
under it in the explorer, and the `$` sorts it to the top. It has no other
purpose and no other content.

To enable, add the following to your VS Code settings.json and adjust the list
to your own config surface:

```jsonc
"explorer.fileNesting.enabled": true,
"explorer.fileNesting.patterns": {
  "package.json": "-package-lock.json, yarn.lock, pnpm-lock.yaml, bun.lockb, bun.lock",
  // - VS Code nests lockfiles under package.json by default. Prefix with '-' so
  //    package-lock.json nests under $config instead.
  "$config": ".editorconfig, .gitattributes, .gitignore, .npmignore, deno.json, deno.jsonc, deno.lock, package.json, package-lock.json, tsconfig.*"
},
```
